Treat f(x) as function application only.

Morphism application as f(x) was never released, so there is no
migration diagnostic. A variable used as f(x) is an undeclared
function; a const used as f(x) is a const called as a function.
Member types and predicates live on model instances, so f.T in those
positions is undeclared.

Test applying f.T to the wrong member type of the same model, writing
f.T as a type or predicate, and naming a declared non-type on a
morphism.
